      "writtenOn": "2025-11-10T21:23:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this mean the benchmarks cannot be built from within a Chromium checkout any more?\n\nWe need to be able to build the Tint benchmarks in a Chromium checkout for the Chrome perf waterfall.",
      "parentUuid": "f167180a_4886830f",
      "revId": "32e32d12e0f46a058a0af167833dc2d329ace54a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02f527f9_a04fde5b",
        "filename": "BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-10T21:35:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes but No.\n\nThis would prevent the top-level target `//third_party/dawn:benchmarks` from building at the root of a Chromium checkout, but that I believe that is the current state of the GN builds before any of my changes. (Looking at the output of `gn ls out/Default/` in my Chromium checkout I don\u0027t see that target)\n\nThe specific target `//third_party/dawn/src/tint:benchmarks` it wrape is still available in my Chromium checkout, so I assume that is what the waterfall depends on.\n\nIf we want `//third_party/dawn:benchmarks` to be available in a Chromium checkout, I can move it also outside of the guard. I was just replicating the existing behaviour as much as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "be0c030c_c4b26e8d",
      "revId": "32e32d12e0f46a058a0af167833dc2d329ace54a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
